  "group_assessments": [
    {
      "group": "Sumy contact / Trubchevsky owner",
      "actual_evidence": [
        {
          "path": "inventory/m36-35-four-sumy-archive-source-reconciliation.json",
          "sha256": "f61451272d960587abab835c2d89e4986a6b0304328c3e46b189a358e903c02d",
          "finding": "Exact single-record source comparison: the simplified UKR Sumy feature reproduces this contact, full UKR Sumy record covers this key, and full RUS Trubchevsky record excludes it. This is the fourth member of a four-center row; the other three in that row have the reverse full-source membership, so this key is distinct and must not inherit their pattern. UKR archive row 7 is Sumy Oblast (UA-59), record hash 1dd44679003e38556eaf5b5cce59f7a393e02a7ad0271b94ea0e841d9249b74d; RUS archive row 1872 is Trubchevsky District ID 1241910, record hash 46c39f7fb3db2408c97a59a6c916aa15deb939bd711884948c829c009abb679a. The saved archive comparison is exact-key only, not a full-family scan."
        },
        {
          "path": "inventory/rus-ukr61-treaty-54132/sumy-155620-osm-history/assessment.json",
          "sha256": "e3fa08b104fb39fcbe6ec9c78c691d97e5cd49145abb2fefdf5099efa1570e11",
          "finding": "The public OSM relation 1241910 history contains 36 versions; v25 is dated 2017-11-20 and names Trubchevsky District with the expected administrative tags. This corroborates relation identity/name and source-era role, not geometric identity of the retained geoBoundaries RUS polygon. The versioned relation XML has 40 members. The historical `/relation/1241910/25/full` endpoint returned HTTP 404 (5,046 bytes); no full geometry was recovered from that response."
        },
        {
          "path": "inventory/rus-ukr61-treaty-54132/n36-128-four-sumy-key-followup.json",
          "sha256": "6347a3f29fa268769d547a713b46cff4dda4f4b7ba54a9dd5f53b7a45b3a6a63",
          "finding": "On sheet N-36-128-В, the key plots near the 242–243 forest-path corridor only under an approximate frame fit. Annex 1 says that path remains on the Russian Federation side, but the visible route/path/terrain strokes overlap and this check did not establish an exact side for the four centers."
        },
        {
          "path": "inventory/rus-ukr61-treaty-54132/n36-128-four-sumy-grid-control-check.json",
          "sha256": "e14b0f99becd5e3169623255807e6424521a572f988f481e8b45b7c68abfd58e",
          "finding": "The sheet’s 1942 frame can be conditionally interpreted as Pulkovo 1942 / Gauss–Kruger zone 6 at this longitude. Inspected local grid strokes are not legibly labeled with projected coordinates; darkness maxima are not reliable controls."
        },
        {
          "path": "inventory/rus-ukr61-treaty-54132/n36-128-four-sumy-native-control-followup.json",
          "sha256": "fcad294896b0ca397940a5e4a9c0968258ce6467396bab6b327045efc1ba76fd",
          "finding": "Higher-resolution composite inspection confirmed nearby map ink but did not provide a labeled interior control, exact route centerline, or independent holdout. No side conclusion was made."
        }
      ],
      "research_assessment": "Substantial, exact-key effort exists: original simplified contact reproduction, both exact full archive memberships, source-era OSM relation history, and the actual treaty text/map corridor and higher-resolution local-control inspection. The evidence conflicts at this key. It supports a narrowly researched-unresolved proposal with the original native hold unchanged; it does not support positive RUS assignment or present-day legal conclusions. The corrected original owner index is 38470 (not 38297).",
      "remaining_limit_not_exhaustion": "Relation v25 confirms source identity but not the retained polygon’s construction. The failed historical full endpoint is recorded; reconstructing that relation version from its archived way/node members could be a future finite source-lineage check if needed. This proposal does not claim every possible source-history route was exhausted."
    },
    {
      "group": "Tarasovsky / Luhansk contact",
      "actual_evidence": [
        {
          "path": "inventory/rus-ukr61-treaty-54132/tarasovsky-five-key-source-record-and-map-review.json",
          "sha256": "7039f0f83fa8ec246d66c6dc1bb11fe05171d3990552cf76780c1aa0559780bd",
          "finding": "Within the exact five-key source study, first three centers are inside full RUS Tarasovsky and outside full UKR Luhansk, but these two are opposite: simplified and full UKR Luhansk cover them; full RUS Tarasovsky excludes them. Exact RUS archive ID 1526041 (ADM2, Tarasovsky District), row 2210, shape hash 460b25523692e2eabea02a827b096100affbf2e8a9bbdfdaa5980b6586fc5136; exact UKR Luhansk UA-09 row 9, shape hash 0501e7df5f0ac4277a4ff8b36a39e0a6fa61f41c33a730ee2ba3ba8f7a828b43. Both archive geometries are valid EPSG:4326 and were compared without repair/buffer."
        },
        {
          "path": "inventory/rus-ukr61-treaty-54132/tarasovsky-two-contrary-keys-route-control-followup.json",
          "sha256": "44f568d34bea29ce044bc91d013da0099fff6a11493fa006fdbd372ca9339ece",
          "finding": "Treaty Annex 1 points 1101–1113 describe Bondarnaya Ravine, control 94.4, Derkul River, and a downstream route. A conditional zone-7 frame fit placed the centers near an engineered reservoir edge; the four frame picks have no independent fit residual or accuracy estimate. The earlier local crops could not identify a numbered node/control or a unique Derkul channel."
        },
        {
          "path": "inventory/rus-ukr61-treaty-54132/tarasovsky-whole-sheet-route-control-search.json",
          "sha256": "6f64f0f841637a01cc0d59f5e5181e132005b965266ebc18a17306d74b2876db",
          "finding": "A further actual whole-sheet read inspected the 2210×2600 page, its full north belt, reservoir-adjacent focus, neighboring rendered crops, and the PDF’s native 2550×3000 JP2 image and local native crop. The title is M-37-128-А (1:50,000, coordinate system 1942 unspecified, terrain 1990, edition 2002); M-37-116-Б at the upper edge is the adjacent sheet index. Nearby visible elevation labels 84.0, 87.2, 80.4, 70.3, 70.8, 56.2, 56.4, 100.3 and 101 did not identify geodetic control 94.4. I found no uniquely identifiable Derkul course or treaty-node sequence in the inspected regions. Multiple engineered shore/canal, rail, road and topographic strokes make an unlabelled blue edge unsuitable as the treaty river. The 15/13 raster scale relation was checked; the registration was not upgraded."
        }
      ],
      "research_assessment": "The exact same-release full-source comparison is contrary to the RUS owner, and the treaty source is relevant but not precisely tied to these centers. The actual whole-sheet/ native-resolution check made the reasonable retained-map step concrete and did not locate a reliable control or river identity. Taken together, this supports a narrowly researched-unresolved proposal for these two cells, with native holds unchanged; it does not justify a positive RUS repair, current-sovereignty statement, or claim that all source-lineage research is exhausted.",
      "remaining_limit_not_exhaustion": "A future finite provenance check could determine whether the full RUS ADM2 archive feature ID 1526041 is directly linked to a specific OSM relation/version and whether that source geometry is recoverable. The current evidence confirms OSM/Wambacher 2017 represented-source context but not capture-date geometry equivalence. This remains a source-version question, not a universal certificate requirement."
    },
    {
      "group": "Krasnosulinsky / Luhansk contact",
      "actual_evidence": [
        {
          "path": "inventory/rus-ukr61-treaty-54132/krasnosulinsky-two-key-independent-assessment-20261023.json",
          "sha256": "c9c3e9ff5cdefbec039019d81f170c22f5dc6677c04a88e1ba7dcbb580ff67ca",
          "finding": "Exact full-source record comparison: UKR Luhansk ADM1 covers both centers; RUS Krasnosulinsky ADM2 excludes both. RUS row 581, ID 1517228, 3,236 points, valid EPSG:4326, record hash 5fb40972e2dd94a7fe11950f78d83801d335af6e7b8783873f96a20adf156c52. UKR row 9 UA-09, 5,146 points, valid EPSG:4326, record hash 0501e7df5f0ac4277a4ff8b36a39e0a6fa61f41c33a730ee2ba3ba8f7a828b43."
        },
        {
          "path": "inventory/rus-ukr61-treaty-54132/krasnosulinsky-two-key-conditional-map-registration.json",
          "sha256": "7bf5ddfc84980c621b650ec9835c4dcb1d27a408a9bc4ab352bc4b88af937261",
          "finding": "A conditional four-corner fit interprets the sheet's generic 1942 label as Pulkovo 1942 / Gauss–Kruger zone 7. It places the centers around x=1314.29,y=687.97 and x=1281.20,y=710.04 pixels, west of the numbered 1209–1212 line on the Ukraine-labeled side in the contextual review. Offsets are hand-read, not exact geodetic measurements; no independent holdout validates the four-corner fit."
        },
        {
          "path": "inventory/rus-ukr61-treaty-54132/krasnosulinsky-two-key-whole-sheet-context-20261023.json",
          "sha256": "fc48ac6f2367dccb088aaddb6e788ed21729cbc040aa00a86266bcb8322c3f6b",
          "finding": "The entire retained M-37-140-Г sheet was visually inspected; it identifies Ukraine/Luhansk and Russia/Rostov on opposite sides and shows the numbered 1209–1212 corridor. Treaty text 4707–4716 describes 1211–1212 along a country road/forest edge and later 1216–1217 explicitly on a narrow forest strip remaining in Ukraine. The later clause is not transferred as an exact local point-side claim."
        }
      ],
      "research_assessment": "The full same-release source comparison is directly adverse to the RUS owner. The actual treaty map/text provide consistent historical Ukraine-side context under a stated conditional registration, with transparent uncertainty. This is substantive, source-specific evidence supporting a narrow researched-unresolved proposal for the two keys while preserving native holds. It is not a positive repair, a current-border determination, or root acceptance.",
      "remaining_limit_not_exhaustion": "The actual fit has no independent geodetic holdout and the exact original-source geometry capture date/lineage is not established. Those limits are disclosed; no additional already-retained evidence identified in this review resolves the conflicting full-source point memberships. A more precise georeferencing/source-version record could refine the historical map relationship but is not treated as a universal precondition to recording researched-unresolved."
    }
  ],
